% ============================================================================
% eye-parts.query.adj — a worked recall over the anatomy eye-parts library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does the retina do?":
% it states no anatomy fact — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks
% binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `eye_part_function`
% rows and returns the function + the table's source/locator/trust. The fourth
% query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the function focuses_light, recall the
% part that does it — the lens). The eardrum has no grounded row here (it is an
% EAR part, not an eye part), so a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine
% never invents a function.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli eye-parts.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "eye-parts.adj"

? eye_part_function(retina, $F)      % expect turns_light_into_signals
? eye_part_function(cornea, $F)      % expect bends_light
? eye_part_function(optic_nerve, $F) % expect carries_signals_to_brain
? eye_part_function($P, focuses_light) % expect lens — reverse recall
? eye_part_function(eardrum, $F)     % expect abstain — eardrum has no row
